---
title: "Answer a question in R and keep the result in SQL"
output: rmarkdown::html_vignette
vignette: >
  %\VignetteIndexEntry{Answer a question in R and keep the result in SQL}
  %\VignetteEngine{knitr::rmarkdown}
  %\VignetteEncoding{UTF-8}
---

```{r setup, include = FALSE}
source("tools/guides/setup.R")
```

You want an agent to analyse a dataset and leave the result somewhere it can
be found later, by you or by another agent. The agent computes in its R
session and keeps what matters as a table in the project's SQL workspace,
`.pi/ducknng/workspace.duckdb`. The R session ends with the conversation; the
table does not.

## The analysis

```{r, echo = FALSE, results = "asis"}
agent_task("
  Using `datasets::airquality`, find which month had the highest mean ozone
  level, ignoring missing readings. Compute it in R and keep the monthly means
  in the SQL workspace as a table `ozone_by_month` with columns `month` and
  `mean_ozone`. Answer in two sentences.
")
```

## The table outlives the agent

The agent has exited. Any DuckDB client can open the workspace file and read
the table it left:

```{r}
workspace_sql("SELECT month, round(mean_ozone, 1) AS mean_ozone FROM ozone_by_month ORDER BY month")
```

## A later session builds on it

A new Pi session in the same project starts with an empty R process, but the
workspace still holds the table. This agent is asked a follow-up question and
told nothing about how the first one worked:

```{r, echo = FALSE, results = "asis"}
agent_task("
  The SQL workspace has a table `ozone_by_month` from an earlier analysis of
  `datasets::airquality`. By how much did the worst month's mean ozone exceed
  the best month's? Answer from that table in one sentence.
")
```

```{r, include = FALSE}
months <- workspace_sql("SELECT month, mean_ozone FROM ozone_by_month")
expected <- aggregate(Ozone ~ Month, data = datasets::airquality, FUN = mean)
stopifnot(
  nrow(months) == 5L,
  isTRUE(all.equal(sort(months$mean_ozone), sort(expected$Ozone), tolerance = 1e-6))
)
```

```{r, echo = FALSE, results = "asis"}
cat("> GUIDE_WORKSPACE_VERIFIED: the monthly means match R's own and persist after the agent exits\n")
```
